    </node>
    <node id="Yue Kingdom">
      <data key="d0">Yue Kingdom</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Yue Kingdom was a neighboring state to Wu, led by King Goujian, and engaged in conflict with Wu.&lt;SEP&gt;Yue Kingdom is a state seeking to avenge its grievances against Wu and improve its sword-making capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Yue Kingdom is the realm ruled by Goujian, engaged in rivalry with the Wu Kingdom.&lt;SEP&gt;The Yue Kingdom is ruled by Goujian and is involved in strategic conflicts with the Wu Kingdom.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6f4631a6bc7286dd9560f06b9845d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b2a680eed881fd86d938031d895d21e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3e590b3ab7f94ee3770d3739196401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a72fd2ce03a23a58c65d98d2258f3e1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1777374824</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Wu Kingdom">
      <data key="d0">Wu Kingdom</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Wu Kingdom was a powerful state in ancient China, rivaling Yue and led by King Fuchai during the events described.&lt;SEP&gt;The Wu Kingdom is a region involved in conflicts with other states and the site of sword forging activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Wu Kingdom is a rival state to Yue, known for its skilled swordsmen and strategic control over resources like tin.&lt;SEP&gt;The Wu Kingdom is the rival state of Yue, known for its skilled warriors and use of Sun Tzu's military strategies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6f4631a6bc7286dd9560f06b9845d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b2a680eed881fd86d938031d895d21e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3e590b3ab7f94ee3770d3739196401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a72fd2ce03a23a58c65d98d2258f3e1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
